# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58): `REQ-ASK` is checked "after load (a load refusal outranks it)". The reality
# declares y twice, so it doesn't load (L §8.3 `LOAD-DUP`), and the request also names zz, which doesn't exist: the
# load refusal prints, not `REQ-ASK`. (A twin: so on tally 2.1.2's refcore too.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input y: int
input y: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  y = 1

ask q: y
=== expect zz
refused: LOAD-DUP ...
